more|additional-before-noun|DETERMINER|Additional quantity before a noun|A greater or additional number or amount of the thing named.|thêm; nhiều hơn|We need more string to hang the remaining decorations.|Chúng tôi cần thêm dây để treo những đồ trang trí còn lại.|More plus plural countable or uncountable noun; more chairs, more water. Compare with much or many.|0
more|additional-standing-alone|PRONOUN|Additional quantity standing alone|An additional amount or number when the thing involved is understood.|thêm; nhiều hơn|There are biscuits on the tray if you would like more.|Có bánh quy trên khay nếu bạn muốn lấy thêm.|Can stand alone; some more, a few more, more of them. The noun need not be repeated.|1
more|greater-degree|ADVERB|Greater degree|To a greater extent, often forming a comparison with an adjective or adverb.|hơn; nhiều hơn|The revised instructions explain the process more clearly.|Hướng dẫn đã sửa giải thích quy trình rõ ràng hơn.|More plus longer adjective or adverb; more useful, more slowly. Avoid double comparatives such as more easier.|2
pedestrian|person-on-foot|NOUN|Person on foot|A person travelling on foot, especially near traffic.|người đi bộ|The driver waited while the pedestrians crossed the entrance.|Người lái xe chờ trong lúc những người đi bộ băng qua lối vào.|Countable; a pedestrian, a pedestrian crossing. The adjective pedestrian has other uses beyond this noun.|-
somewhat|moderate-small-degree|ADVERB|To a limited degree|To a degree that is noticeable but not very great.|hơi; phần nào|The second design is somewhat simpler than the first.|Thiết kế thứ hai có phần đơn giản hơn thiết kế đầu tiên.|Often modifies an adjective or comparative; somewhat unusual. More formal than a bit.|0
wildlife|wild-animals-collectively|NOUN|Wild animals collectively|Animals that live in natural surroundings rather than being kept as domestic animals.|động vật hoang dã|Visitors watched the wildlife from the path without approaching the animals.|Du khách quan sát động vật hoang dã từ lối đi mà không đến gần chúng.|Uncountable; local wildlife, protect wildlife. Use wild animals for a countable plural phrase.|0
dog|domestic-canine|NOUN|Domestic canine|A domestic animal related to wolves, commonly kept as a companion or trained for work.|con chó|Their dog carried a soft toy to the garden gate.|Con chó của họ mang một món đồ chơi mềm đến cổng vườn.|Countable; a dog, dogs. A puppy is a young dog.|0
